SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and an enum is code: use a const object, as in const Color = { Red: 0, Green: 1 } as const
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and a parameter property is code: declare the field and assign it in the constructor, as in who: string; constructor(who: string) { this.who = who }
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and import x = require(…) is code: write const x = require("…")
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and import x = require(…) is code: write import x from "…"
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and import x = require(…) is code: write const x = require("…") in CommonJS, or import x from "…" in an ES module
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and a namespace with values is code (an older Node, such as 22.13, refuses even one with only types): use a module of its own (a file) or an object, as in const NS = { x: 1 }
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and a <T>x cast is code: write x as T
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and an enum is code: use a const object, as in const Color = { Red: 0, Green: 1 } as const
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and export = is code: write module.exports = x
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and export = is code: write export default x
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and export = is code: write module.exports = x in CommonJS, or export default x in an ES module
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and a parameter property is code: declare the field and assign it in the constructor, as in who: string; constructor(who: string) { this.who = who }
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and a namespace with values is code (an older Node, such as 22.13, refuses even one with only types): use a module of its own (a file) or an object, as in const NS = { x: 1 }
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and import x = require(…) is code: write const x = require("…")
SyntaxError | Node runs TypeScript by removing its types, and export = is code: write @export { x }
